  "worked_solution": "The set  $P\u2216S$ is the set of all elements belonging to $P$ but *not* $S.$ Note that the elements $\u25fb,\u2662,\u2661\\in P$ are also in $S,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P\u2216S & =P-S \\\\  & ={\u2660,\u25fb,\u2662,\u2661}-{\u2662,\u25b3,\u2663,\u25fb,\u2661} \\\\  & ={\u2660}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
